<%# One person's share on the quick split screen. Rendered by the server for the
    rows that exist when the page loads, and cloned by QuickSplitLogic from the
    <template> below it for the rows the stepper adds. Either way the markup
    lives here, in ERB, and not in JavaScript.

    The em dash is the "no amount yet" state. tabular-nums keeps the figures the
    same width so the column does not jitter while the organizer types. %>
<li class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-black/20 py-3">
  <span data-share-row-name><%= "Person #{position}" %></span>
  <span class="font-medium tabular-nums" data-share-row-amount>&mdash;</span>
</li>
